\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Perfect life of love!
\par All, all is finished now,
\par All that He left His throne above
\par To do for us below.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. No work is left undone
\par Of all the Father willed;
\par His toils and sorrows, one by one,
\par The Scriptures have fulfilled.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. No pain that we can share
\par But He has felt its smart;
\par All forms of human grief and care
\par Have pierced that tender heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And on His thorn-crowned head,
\par And on His sinless soul,
\par Our sins in all their guilt were laid,
\par That He might make us whole.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. In perfect love He dies;
\par For me He dies, for me!
\par O all-atoning Sacrifice,
\par I cling by faith to Thee
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. In every time of need,
\par Before the judgement throne,
\par Thy work, O Lamb of God, I'll plead,
\par Thy merits, not my own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Yet work, O Lord, in me,
\par As Thou for me hast wrought;
\par And let my love the answer be
\par To grace Thy love has brought.
\par                                         Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

